  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "氣候調適",
    "sub_ename": "CLIMATE ADAPTATION",
    "describe_ch": "在當代全球氣候變遷日益劇烈的背景下，極端氣候事件、海平面上升、旱澇災害與生態衝擊已成為人類社會與自然系統所共同面臨的重大挑戰。本課程旨在培養學生具備理解氣候變遷趨勢、辦識氣候風險，以及因應與調適的跨領域整合能力。\r\n課程將從氣候變遷的科學基礎出發，探討氣候變遷的成因與影響，進而介紹全球與地方層級的減緩(mitigation)與調適(adaptation)策略。學生將學習如何分析氣候風險與脆弱度評估方法，並理解在面對災害時，不同領域(如水資源、都市規劃、農業、公共衛生等)所採取的防災與調適行為。",
    "describe_eh": "Against the backdrop of increasingly severe global climate change, extreme climate events, rising sea levels, droughts and floods, and ecological shocks have become major challenges faced by by both human society and the natural system. This course aims to cultivate students' cross-disciplinary integration capabilities in understanding climate change trends, identifying climate risks, and coping and adapting.\r\nThe course will start from the scientific basis of climate change, explore the causes and impacts of climate change, and then introduce mitigation and adaptation strategies at the global and local levels. Students will learn how to analyze climate risk and vulnerability assessment methods, and understand the disaster prevention and adaptation behaviors taken by different fields (such as water resources, urban planning, agriculture, public health, etc.) when facing disasters.",
